    "body": "Thanks! This is a good start. Let's structure this slightly differently however. I'm thinking something like:\n\n> When a script invokes the importScripts(urls) method on a WorkerGlobalScope object, the user agent must import scripts into worker global scope, with the following options:\n> - To validate the state, ...\n> - To get a fetch result, ...\n> - To postprocess the fetch result, ...\n\n(notice my slight renaming of the hooks)\n\nThen, after this, similar to what you've already got, you say:\n\n> The import scripts into worker global scope algorithm has three hooks...\n> \n> To import scripts into worker global scope, the user agent must run the following steps:...\n\n---\n\nAlso, not a big deal but try to follow the commit message guidelines from [writing good commit messages](https://github.com/erlang/otp/wiki/Writing-good-commit-messages).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
